# Per-player plan-name sequences

Regress automatic naming so only saved plans of the same kind and player advance a default name.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] `Card plan 2` is proposed only when the selected player already has `Card plan 1`.
- [x] `Con plan 2` is proposed only when the selected player already has `Con plan 1`.
- [x] A Constructions plan never advances the Cards sequence, and a Cards plan never advances the Constructions sequence.
- [x] Plans belonging to another player never advance the selected player's sequence.
- [x] The first unused positive exact default name is selected within the relevant player/kind collection.
- [x] Unrelated custom names and cancelled unsaved drafts do not advance a sequence.
- [x] Existing user-entered names are never rewritten.
- [x] Unit and UI regression coverage compiles for both kinds and multiple players.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- This clarifies and supersedes any ambiguous cross-kind reading of REQ-014 and verifies TASK-016's intended behavior.

## Evidence

- Audited the pure generator: it filters saved plans by exact player and kind before selecting the first unused positive exact default name.
- Existing unit coverage verifies gaps, unrelated names, both kinds, and multiple players.
- Expanded UI coverage verifies a renamed custom plan does not consume `Card plan 1`, Constructions do not advance Cards, cancelled drafts consume nothing, and Blue starts an independent sequence.
